WEBVTT

00:00:00.059 --> 00:00:02.819
Before joining a shift, read its day detail.

00:00:03.259 --> 00:00:08.199
This recorded example is Training, Academy signup practice, on Tuesday,

00:00:08.199 --> 00:00:12.760
October twenty-seventh, twenty twenty-six, from one until three in the afternoon.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:17.840
These are historical recording dates; use an eligible day for your own practice.

00:00:18.299 --> 00:00:19.940
Open slots shows two.

00:00:20.420 --> 00:00:25.889
Under Open needs, Firehouse fifty-one lists Chief and Needed, two, while

00:00:25.889 --> 00:00:28.069
Roster says no one is on this day yet.

00:00:28.590 --> 00:00:31.469
Check that this is the intended occurrence and appropriate work

00:00:31.469 --> 00:00:33.599
for you, then choose Sign Up.

00:00:33.819 --> 00:00:36.619
Choose your team explains that you are selecting the group you

00:00:36.619 --> 00:00:38.319
are signing up with for this day.

00:00:38.689 --> 00:00:43.770
The example offers Firehouse fifty-one, with Chief, two, and Open, two.

00:00:44.249 --> 00:00:45.940
Its radio choice is selected.

00:00:46.379 --> 00:00:49.110
Review the shift date and time again above the team.

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:52.930
Back returns from this confirmation without submitting this choice.

00:00:53.319 --> 00:00:58.079
When the intended team and occurrence are correct, choose Confirm sign-up once.

00:00:58.189 --> 00:01:02.500
The returned day detail now says You are on, and Open slots

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:04.520
has changed from two to one.

00:01:05.020 --> 00:01:09.870
Under Roster, Firehouse fifty-one contains Wallace Boden with the You label.

00:01:10.239 --> 00:01:13.220
Open needs shows Chief and Needed, one.

00:01:13.689 --> 00:01:15.840
Those are the recorded results of this signup.

00:01:16.489 --> 00:01:20.590
Read the named roster entry as well as the count so you can distinguish your own

00:01:20.590 --> 00:01:22.590
membership from another person's place.

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:26.709
This example returns a rostered result; it does not demonstrate a

00:01:26.709 --> 00:01:29.100
supervisor approving a pending request.

00:01:29.250 --> 00:01:31.660
The same rostered day offers Withdraw.

00:01:32.150 --> 00:01:36.310
Check the title, date and hours before using it, especially when a

00:01:36.310 --> 00:01:38.330
shift name repeats on several days.

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:43.139
Request trade is a separate action on this screen; this exercise removes

00:01:43.139 --> 00:01:46.589
the personal signup instead of asking a colleague to take the shift.

00:01:47.009 --> 00:01:50.429
Follow your department's coverage arrangements before making that change.

00:01:50.829 --> 00:01:53.210
Choose Withdraw to review its confirmation.

00:01:53.469 --> 00:01:57.720
The confirmation asks, Withdraw from this shift, and says you will

00:01:57.720 --> 00:02:00.939
be removed from the roster for Tuesday, October twenty-seventh.

00:02:01.429 --> 00:02:04.320
The shift title and one-to-three time remain above it.

00:02:04.719 --> 00:02:07.849
Back leaves this confirmation without completing the withdrawal.

00:02:08.259 --> 00:02:11.919
Check the intended occurrence before choosing the red Withdraw button to

00:02:11.919 --> 00:02:13.849
carry out this training cancellation.

00:02:14.159 --> 00:02:16.560
The returned detail offers Sign Up again.

00:02:17.040 --> 00:02:22.870
Open slots is two, Open needs again says Chief and Needed, two, and

00:02:22.870 --> 00:02:25.309
Roster says no one is on this day yet.

00:02:25.769 --> 00:02:29.979
The earlier You are on state and named personal entry are absent.

00:02:30.319 --> 00:02:33.479
Compare the returned state with the original occurrence rather

00:02:33.479 --> 00:02:36.309
than assuming that pressing a button completed the change.

00:02:36.709 --> 00:02:40.209
This recording checks the returned day sheet; it does not claim a

00:02:40.209 --> 00:02:43.860
separate cancellation-history record or a supervisor approval.

00:02:44.029 --> 00:02:48.260
These checks help community paramedicine and mental health teams plan outreach

00:02:48.260 --> 00:02:52.609
coverage, search-and-rescue teams fill support shifts, security companies

00:02:52.609 --> 00:02:57.050
staff posts, wildland contractors coordinate crews, and industrial

00:02:57.050 --> 00:02:59.430
response teams arrange standby coverage.

00:02:59.819 --> 00:03:03.100
Fire and EMS departments can use them for station staffing.

00:03:03.680 --> 00:03:08.840
For each setting, verify the occurrence, team needs, your personal roster state

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:11.149
and any required approval process.

00:03:11.579 --> 00:03:15.379
After a signup or withdrawal, read the actual returned result

00:03:15.379 --> 00:03:17.099
before planning coverage around it.
